course: dictionary
lesson: 2326
title: The crowbar and the lever
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A crowbar is a long, heavy metal bar with a flat or bent end. People use it to lift things or to force them open. «A crowbar with a small stone underneath as a pivot can lift a heavy stone slab.» The small stone under the bar is the pivot, the point the bar turns around.
explain: A crowbar is a lever. When you push down on the long end, the short end lifts the heavy load. So a small push gives a big force. «If you push far from the pivot, a small force can lift a heavy load that sits close to the pivot.»
explain: The sentences give you clues. They say the crowbar lifts heavy stones, so it must be strong and heavy itself. Check your meaning by swapping it in: a crowbar is a kind of lever, and a lever is something that lifts a heavy load with a small push.
fact: A crowbar is a long, heavy metal bar with a flat or bent end.
fact: A crowbar is used to lift things or to force things open.
fact: A crowbar works as a lever, so a small push gives a big force.
fact: The pivot is the point a lever turns around, like the small stone under the bar.
fact: Builders use crowbars to pull out nails or lift boards.
exercise: What is a crowbar? | *A long, heavy metal bar with a flat or bent end | A small paper bag for lunch | A soft cloth for cleaning windows
exercise: «A crowbar with a small stone underneath as a pivot can lift a heavy stone slab.» What is the pivot here? | *The small stone underneath the bar | The hammer | The end of the bar you hold | The heavy stone slab
exercise: Why can a crowbar lift something heavy with a small push? | It is made of wood and floats | *It works as a lever, so a small push gives a big force | It is very light and easy to lift | It makes the load disappear
test: What does a crowbar work as? | A magnet | A spring | A pulley | *A lever
test: «If you push far from the pivot, a small force can lift a heavy load that sits close to the pivot.» What does this tell you? | The load becomes lighter and floats | The bar breaks at once | Nothing changes at all | *A small push far from the pivot can lift a heavy load close to it
exam: In a story, a burglar uses a crowbar to force a door open. What is the crowbar used for here? | To paint a wall | *To force something open | To cook dinner | To catch a fish
